// Code signing, without anybody's account details in the repository.
//
// A security-scoped bookmark — the permission the user gives when they point
// the app at a folder — is bound to the app's *code identity*. Ad-hoc signing
// has no certificate, so that identity is the binary's own hash and every
// rebuild throws the permission away (§11, `Design/FAVORITES_SYNC_PLAN.md`).
// Signing with a real identity is what makes a granted folder stay granted.
//
// The team that identity belongs to is personal, so it is not kept here. Put it
// in `Signing.local.xcconfig`, which git ignores:
//
//     DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = <your team>
//     CODE_SIGN_STYLE = Automatic
//     CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY = Apple Development
//
// Find the team with:
//
//     security find-certificate -a -c "Apple Development" -p | openssl x509 -noout -subject
//
// — it is the `OU` field. Without the file the app falls back to ad-hoc
// signing, which builds and runs; only the folder permission stops surviving
// rebuilds.
//
// A team belongs to a person, so it never enters the repository. To keep it
// that way by construction rather than by care, install the hook that refuses
// to commit one:
//
//     git config core.hooksPath Scripts/git-hooks

// The fallback, stated plainly rather than as an interpolation keyed on the
// team. `$(CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY_$(DEVELOPMENT_TEAM:default=none))` was the clever
// version and it was wrong twice over: with a team configured it expanded to
// `CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY_<team>`, which nothing defines, so the identity came out
// **empty** — that is the "isn't code signed but requires entitlements" warning
// — and because the include sat above it, the line overrode the very local
// file it was meant to defer to, so the machine with a real certificate was
// building unsigned and the bookmarks were losing their identity on every
// rebuild anyway.
//
// The include goes last instead: in an xcconfig the later assignment wins, so a
// machine with a local file overrides these two and one without keeps them.
CODE_SIGN_STYLE = Manual
CODE_SIGN_IDENTITY = -

#include? "Signing.local.xcconfig"
